        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): stream heartbeat transcript scans without full-file reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nDoctor heartbeat main-session repair loaded the entire session transcript with `fs.readFileSync` before deciding whether the main session was heartbeat-poisoned. A large JSONL transcript (common after long heartbeat-only ownership) forced the whole file into one string during `openclaw doctor` state integrity. Chunked reads alone were also insufficient if a single JSONL record (or a missing newline) kept growing the carry buffer.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nScan the transcript with a fixed-size sync chunk reader (`openSync` + `readSync` + `StringDecoder`) and cap retained JSONL records at 256 KiB. Oversized incomplete or complete records fail closed (no heartbeat classification / no repair) so memory stays bounded even for malformed transcripts. Keep the call sites synchronous because `resolveHeartbeatMainSessionRepairCandidate` runs inside the session-store update path.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`openclaw doctor --fix` can classify and move heartbeat-owned main sessions even when the transcript is multi-megabyte, without risking an OOM from a single full-file string read or an unbounded carry buffer. Mixed transcripts and oversized single records still block repair.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\n#### Behavior or issue addressed\n\nLarge heartbeat-only transcripts are scanned in chunks; doctor still moves the poisoned main session; a single oversized JSONL record declines repair; the transcript path is never loaded via `readFileSync`.\n\n#### Canonical reachability path\n\n`openclaw doctor --fix --yes` → `noteStateIntegrity` → `repairHeartbeatPoisonedMainSession` → `resolveHeartbeatMainSessionRepairCandidate` → `summarizeTranscriptHeartbeatMessages` (chunked scan + record cap).\n\n#### Real environment tested\n\nLocal trusted source checkout; isolated `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` + `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH` fixture with an ~82 KiB heartbeat-only JSONL (661 heartbeat user turns); focused Vitest for multi-chunk repair and oversized-record decline.\n\n#### Exact steps or command run after this patch\n\n```bash\n# Fixture: OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=<tmp>/state, OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=<tmp>/openclaw.json\n# sessions.json main entry -> cli-proof-heartbeat.jsonl (~82 KiB heartbeat-only JSONL)\nnode ./openclaw.mjs doctor --fix --yes\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-state-integrity.test.ts \\\n  -t \"multi-chunk heartbeat|single JSONL record exceeds\" --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n#### Evidence after fix\n\nReal CLI (`openclaw doctor --fix --yes`) against the isolated fixture:\n\n```text\n◇  State integrity\n│  - Main session agent:main:main appears to be a heartbeat-owned session\n│    (661 heartbeat-only user message(s)).\n│    Doctor can move it to\n│    agent:main:heartbeat-recovered-2026-07-18t14-08-16.517z and let the\n│    next interactive launch create a fresh main session.\n\n◇  Doctor changes\n│  - Moved heartbeat-owned main session agent:main:main to\n│    agent:main:heartbeat-recovered-2026-07-18t14-08-16.517z.\n\nDoctor complete.\n```\n\nPost-run store keys:\n\n```text\nBEFORE: agent:main:main\nAFTER:  agent:main:heartbeat-recovered-2026-07-18t14-08-16.517z\n        main=missing\n        sid=cli-proof-heartbeat\ndoctor_exit=0\n```\n\nFocused Vitest:\n\n```text\n✓ repairs a multi-chunk heartbeat transcript without loading it via readFileSync 134ms\n✓ declines repair when a single JSONL record exceeds the scanner record cap 62ms\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed | 33 skipped (35)\n```\n\n#### Observed result after fix\n\nMulti-chunk heartbeat transcripts repair via real doctor CLI; oversized single JSONL records decline classification and leave `agent:main:main` in place; mixed transcripts still block repair.\n\n#### What was not tested\n\nInteractive TTY doctor prompts; multi-GB live operator state directories outside the isolated fixture.\n\n#### Fix classification\n\nbugfix — unbounded transcript/record retention during doctor heartbeat repair\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nAI-assisted. Author reviewed the production caller path, CLI fixture output, and focused proof.\n",
